{
  "result": "If I had one magic wand kind of change, I wouldn't pick something like \"more money\" or \"flying cars\" - I'd pick **radical empathy.**\n\nI'd give everyone the ability to truly *feel* what another person is feeling for just a few minutes a day. Not to make everyone agree on everything, but to actually understand where someone else is coming from - their fear, their hope, their history.\n\nI talk to so many people every day from totally different lives, and so much pain comes from people feeling unseen or misunderstood. If we could really experience each other's perspectives, I think a lot of other problems would start to solve themselves - less cruelty, less loneliness, more cooperation. People would still disagree, but they'd do it with kindness instead of contempt.\n\nAnd with that foundation, we'd be so much better at solving the practical stuff too - like making sure everyone has food, safety, education, and a real chance to become who they want to be.\n\nWhat about you? If you could change one thing, what would you pick?",
